{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneElectronBlockExact","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KeystoneElectronBlockExact","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.BWVacuumRowConcrete"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete_electron_block_exact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete_electron_block_exact","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneElectronBlockExact.lean#L82-L93","doc":"**The electron block `[3,1,1]` — keystone gate exact at real `q₀`, framing-free.**\n`[3,1,1]` is self-conjugate (`c = 0+1+2−1−2 = 0`), so its keystone vacuum-row value equals the Hecke\nmodular datum `S₀ = d_q/D` **exactly** — no continuation from the root-of-unity fibre.  (Its closed\nvalue is `d_q([3,1,1]) = [3]_q[4]_q/[2]_q`, `KeystoneMcKayValueMap.qFactorial_shape_311`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete_selfConj_exact","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.bwS0Concrete_selfConj_exact","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneElectronBlockExact.lean#L67-L80","doc":"**The de-opaqued keystone gate is EXACT on the self-conjugate sector, for every framing.**\nOn a self-conjugate block the twist is trivial (`theta_selfConj_eq_one`), so `θ_λ^f = 1^f = 1` for\nall `f`, and `bwS0Concrete_of_twist_pow_one` gives `bwS0Concrete = S₀` with **no archimedean\ncontinuation** — the framing obstruction that refutes the gate off-diagonal is absent here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.theta_selfConj_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.theta_selfConj_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneElectronBlockExact.lean#L59-L65","doc":"**The twist is trivial on a self-conjugate block: `θ_λ = 1` for every `q`.**  Immediate from\n`c(λ) = 0` (`selfConj_contentSum_zero`) and `q^0 = 1` — no `q₀ > 1`, no root-of-unity fibre. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.selfConj_contentSum_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Keystone.selfConj_contentSum_zero","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KeystoneElectronBlockExact.lean#L50-L57","doc":"**Self-conjugate ⇒ zero content sum.**  The content sum is transpose-antisymmetric\n(`contentSum_conjugate`, `c(λ′) = − c(λ)`); on a self-conjugate block `λ′ = λ` this gives\n`c(λ) = − c(λ)`, so `c(λ) = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}